{#
 # Log Level Row Styles
 #
 # Tints data rows by log level using the `logLevel` color set from base
 # `ColorHelper`. Single layer per state, no JavaScript, no stacking.
 #
 # Mechanism — mirrors Craft's native cp-table pattern:
 #   - The `<tr>` carries the left-border indicator + the `--hover-bg-color`
 #     custom property (same variable Craft sets on `table.data tbody tr`).
 #   - The `<td>` inherits the variable from its parent `<tr>` and paints
 #     its background from it.
 #   - Craft's `:hover` rule on TD reads the same variable for free.
 #
 # Selector form: a `lr-level-{level}` class on the parent `<tr>` drives all
 # rules. Use cp-table's `rowClassKey` to inject the class from a precomputed
 # field on the row data (e.g., `tableConfig.rowClassKey = 'levelClass'`
 # where each row has `levelClass: 'lr-level-error'`).
 #
 # Three intensity tiers + a darker border for the active region:
 #   Resting  → faint cell tint, subtle border (data rows at rest)
 #   Active   → stronger cell tint, darker border (parent row on hover or
 #              expanded — visual focal point of the active region)
 #   Context  → resting-equivalent cell tint, darker border (the expanded
 #              child row; subordinate body inside the active region)
 #
 # The bg-alpha hierarchy creates a focal expanded row that stands out
 # against both resting siblings and its own context body, while the
 # darker border on hover/expanded/context visually groups them as
 # one "active region."
 #
 # States covered:
 #   - Resting:        .lr-data-row.lr-level-X > td
 #                     → rgba(level, bgAlpha)
 #                     → border rgba(level, borderAlpha)
 #   - Hover:          Craft's native rule on TD reads --hover-bg-color
 #                     → rgba(level, bgActiveAlpha)
 #                     + our :hover rule on TR
 #                     → border rgba(level, borderActiveAlpha)
 #   - Expanded:       .lr-data-row.lr-level-X.lr-row-expanded > td
 #                     (.lr-row-expanded toggled by cp-table's click-to-expand JS)
 #                     → rgba(level, bgActiveAlpha)
 #                     → border rgba(level, borderActiveAlpha)
 #   - Context row:    .lr-context-row reads inherited --hover-bg-color
 #                     and shares the parent's border-left for alignment
 #                     → rgba(level, bgContextAlpha)
 #                     → border rgba(level, borderActiveAlpha)
 #
 # Earlier implementation used `:has(td[data-level="X"])` to derive row tint
 # from a cell attribute. Switched to a class on the `<tr>` to eliminate the
 # per-row `:has()` selector matching, which becomes a paint/layout bottleneck
 # on large tables (>500 rows).
 #
 # Usage:
 # {% include 'lindemannrock-base/_partials/styles-log-level-rows' %}
 #
 # With custom alpha values:
 # {% include 'lindemannrock-base/_partials/styles-log-level-rows' with {
 #     bgAlpha: 0.05,
 #     bgActiveAlpha: 0.12,
 # } only %}
 #
 # Parameters (all optional):
 # - bgAlpha (default 0.10): resting cell tint alpha
 # - bgActiveAlpha (default 0.15): hover / expanded tint alpha (focal point)
 # - bgContextAlpha (default 0.07): context-row tint alpha (subordinate body)
 # - borderAlpha (default 0.30): resting left-border alpha
 # - borderActiveAlpha (default 0.70): hover / expanded / context border alpha
 #}

{% set logLevels = lrColorSet('logLevel') %}
{% set bgAlpha = bgAlpha ?? 0.10 %}
{% set bgActiveAlpha = bgActiveAlpha ?? 0.15 %}
{% set bgContextAlpha = bgContextAlpha ?? 0.07 %}
{% set borderAlpha = borderAlpha ?? 0.30 %}
{% set borderActiveAlpha = borderActiveAlpha ?? 0.70 %}

<style>
{% for level, palette in logLevels %}
    /* Parent row resting: subtle border + active-state variable */
    .lr-data-row.lr-level-{{ level }} {
        border-left: 3px solid rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ borderAlpha }});
        --hover-bg-color: rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ bgActiveAlpha }});
    }
    /* Parent row resting cell tint */
    .lr-data-row.lr-level-{{ level }} > td {
        background-color: rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ bgAlpha }});
    }
    /* Parent row hover — border darkens to match active state */
    .lr-data-row.lr-level-{{ level }}:hover {
        border-left-color: rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ borderActiveAlpha }});
    }
    /* Parent row expanded — TD bg matches hover intensity, border stays dark */
    .lr-data-row.lr-level-{{ level }}.lr-row-expanded {
        border-left-color: rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ borderActiveAlpha }});
    }
    .lr-data-row.lr-level-{{ level }}.lr-row-expanded > td {
        background-color: rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ bgActiveAlpha }});
    }
    /* Context row: darker border (unifies the active region with the
       expanded parent) + lighter bg via the inherited variable */
    .lr-data-row.lr-level-{{ level }} + .lr-context-row {
        border-left: 3px solid rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ borderActiveAlpha }});
        --hover-bg-color: rgba({{ palette.rgb }}, {{ bgContextAlpha }});
    }
{% endfor %}

    /* Context row td paints from the inherited --hover-bg-color variable,
       scoped to context rows that follow a level-marked data row. */
    .lr-data-row[class*="lr-level-"] + .lr-context-row > td {
        background-color: var(--hover-bg-color);
    }
    .lr-data-row td {
        vertical-align: top;
    }
</style>
